  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Zn</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>Na</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>ZnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8593;</mo></math></p><p>In the above reaction, Zinc reacts with Sodium Hydroxide,&nbsp;gives Sodium Zincate with evolving of hydrogen. Here&nbsp;Zn does not react as an acid in the reaction above since the reaction is not an acid-base one, but rather oxidation-reduction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>ZnO</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> is anhydrous form of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Zn</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math></p></blockquote>",
